WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.272
One-hot encoding creates separate indicator columns.

00:00:03.272 --> 00:00:09.797
With Bronze as the reference category, the generated columns represent Silver, Gold, and Platinum.

00:00:09.797 --> 00:00:12.587
Bronze is represented by all zeros.

00:00:12.587 --> 00:00:18.352
This is useful when we do not want a model to treat categories as points on one numeric

00:00:18.352 --> 00:00:20.692
line. The tradeoff is dimensionality.

00:00:20.692 --> 00:00:24.702
Variables with many categories can create many columns.

00:00:24.702 --> 00:00:30.132
Preprocessing is not neutral: it tells software how to interpret the variable.

00:00:30.132 --> 00:00:37.147
One-hot encoding avoids inventing rank for nominal categories; ordinal coding preserves a known order;

00:00:37.147 --> 00:00:42.087
scaling changes numerical representation but not conceptual meaning.

00:00:42.087 --> 00:00:49.343
In predictive work, learned preprocessing should be fitted only on training data so evaluation remains honest.
